#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:1
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Introduction for people new to both FreeBSD and UNIX®"
msgstr "为同时刚接触 FreeBSD 和 UNIX® 的人编写的介绍"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:1
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "For People New to Both FreeBSD and UNIX®"
msgstr "写给同时刚接触 FreeBSD 和 UNIX® 的人"

#. type: Title =
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:11
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "For People New to Both FreeBSD and UNIX(R)"
msgstr "写给同时刚接触 FreeBSD 和 UNIX(R) 的人"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:43
msgid "Abstract"
msgstr "摘要"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:45
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Congratulations on installing FreeBSD! This introduction is for people new "
"to both FreeBSD _and_ UNIX(R)-so it starts with basics."
msgstr "恭喜您安装了 FreeBSD！本介绍面向同时刚接触 FreeBSD __和__ UNIX(R) 的人——因此将从基础知识讲起。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:47
msgid "'''"
msgstr "'''"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:51
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Logging in and Getting Out"
msgstr "登录和退出"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:57
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Log in (when you see `login:`) as a user you created during installation or "
"as `root`.  (Your FreeBSD installation will already have an account for "
"`root`; who can go anywhere and do anything, including deleting essential "
"files, so be careful!)  The symbols % and # in the following stand for the "
"prompt (yours may be different), with % indicating an ordinary user and # "
"indicating `root`."
msgstr "看到 `login:` 提示符时，请使用安装期间创建的用户帐户或 `root` 登录。（您的 FreeBSD 安装中已经有一个 `root` 帐户；它可以访问任何地方并执行任何操作，包括删除重要文件，因此请务必小心！）以下示例中的 % 和 # 表示提示符（您的提示符可能不同），其中 % 表示普通用户，# 表示 `root`。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:59
#, fuzzy
msgid "To log out (and get a new `login:` prompt) type"
msgstr "要注销（并重新显示 `login:` 提示符），请输入"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:63
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# exit\n"
msgstr "# exit\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:67
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"as often as necessary.  Yes, press kbd:[enter] after commands, and remember "
"that UNIX(R) is case-sensitive-``exit``, not `EXIT`."
msgstr "根据需要重复此操作。是的，输入命令后请按 kbd:[enter]，并记住 UNIX(R) 区分大小写——是 ``exit``，而不是 `EXIT`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:69
#, fuzzy
msgid "To shut down the machine type"
msgstr "要关闭计算机，请输入"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:73
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# /sbin/shutdown -h now\n"
msgstr "# /sbin/shutdown -h now\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:76
#, fuzzy
msgid "Or to reboot type"
msgstr "要重新启动，请输入"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:80
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# /sbin/shutdown -r now\n"
msgstr "# /sbin/shutdown -r now\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:83
msgid "or"
msgstr "或"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:87
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# /sbin/reboot\n"
msgstr "# /sbin/reboot\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:93
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You can also reboot with kbd:[Ctrl+Alt+Delete].  Give it a little time to do "
"its work.  This is equivalent to `/sbin/reboot` in recent releases of "
"FreeBSD and is much, much better than hitting the reset button.  You do not "
"want to have to reinstall this thing, do you?"
msgstr "您也可以按 kbd:[Ctrl+Alt+Delete] 重新启动。请稍等片刻，让系统完成操作。在近期版本的 FreeBSD 中，这相当于执行 `/sbin/reboot`，而且比按下重置按钮好得多。您可不想不得不重新安装这个系统吧？"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:95
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Adding a User with Root Privileges"
msgstr "添加具有 root 权限的用户"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:98
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If you did not create any users when you installed the system and are thus "
"logged in as `root`, you should probably create a user now with"
msgstr "如果您安装系统时没有创建任何用户，因此目前是以 `root` 身份登录，最好现在使用以下命令创建一个用户："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:102
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# adduser\n"
msgstr "# adduser\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:108
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The first time you use `adduser`, it might ask for some defaults to save.  "
"You might want to make the default shell man:csh[1] instead of man:sh[1], if "
"it suggests `sh` as the default.  Otherwise just press enter to accept each "
"default.  These defaults are saved in [.filename]#/etc/adduser.conf#, an "
"editable file."
msgstr "第一次使用 `adduser` 时，它可能会询问是否保存一些默认设置。如果它建议将 `sh` 设为默认 shell，您可能会想把默认 shell 改为 man:csh[1]，而不是 man:sh[1]。否则，只需按 Enter 接受每项默认设置。这些默认设置保存在 [.filename]#/etc/adduser.conf# 中；这是一个可编辑的文件。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:112
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Suppose you create a user `jack` with full name _Jack Benimble_.  Give "
"`jack` a password if security (even kids around who might pound on the "
"keyboard) is an issue.  When it asks you if you want to invite `jack` into "
"other groups, type `wheel`"
msgstr "假设您创建了一个名为 `jack`、全名为 __Jack Benimble__ 的用户。如果您在意安全问题（例如家里有孩子可能会乱按键盘），请为 `jack` 设置密码。当系统询问是否要将 `jack` 加入其他组时，请输入 `wheel`："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:116
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Login group is \"jack\". Invite jack into other groups: wheel\n"
msgstr "Login group is \"jack\". Invite jack into other groups: wheel\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:120
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This will make it possible to log in as `jack` and use the man:su[1] command "
"to become `root`.  Then you will not get scolded any more for logging in as "
"`root`."
msgstr "这样，您就可以以 `jack` 身份登录，并使用 man:su[1] 命令切换为 `root`。这样就不会再因为以 `root` 身份登录而受到责备。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:123
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You can quit `adduser` any time by typing kbd:[Ctrl+C], and at the end you "
"will have a chance to approve your new user or simply type kbd:[n] for no.  "
"You might want to create a second new user so that when you edit `jack`'s "
"login files, you will have a hot spare in case something goes wrong."
msgstr "您随时可以按 kbd:[Ctrl+C] 退出 `adduser`；在最后，您可以确认新用户，也可以直接输入 kbd:[n] 表示否。您可能还想创建第二个新用户，这样在编辑 `jack` 的登录文件时，如果出了问题，就有一个备用帐户可用。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:126
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once you have done this, use `exit` to get back to a login prompt and log in "
"as `jack`.  In general, it is a good idea to do as much work as possible as "
"an ordinary user who does not have the power-and risk-of `root`."
msgstr "完成后，使用 `exit` 返回登录提示符，然后以 `jack` 身份登录。通常，尽可能以普通用户身份完成工作是个好主意，因为普通用户不具备 `root` 的权限，也不会承担相应的风险。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:129
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If you already created a user and you want the user to be able to `su` to "
"`root`, you can log in as `root` and edit the file [.filename]#/etc/group#, "
"adding `jack` to the first line (the group `wheel`).  But first you need to "
"practice man:vi[1], the text editor-or use the simpler text editor, man:"
"ee[1], installed on recent versions of FreeBSD."
msgstr "如果您已经创建了一个用户，并希望该用户能够使用 `su` 切换为 `root`，可以以 `root` 身份登录并编辑 [.filename]#/etc/group# 文件，将 `jack` 添加到第一行（即 `wheel` 组）。不过，首先您需要练习使用文本编辑器 man:vi[1]——或者使用近期 FreeBSD 版本中安装的、更简单的文本编辑器 man:ee[1]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:131
#, fuzzy
msgid "To delete a user, use `rmuser`."
msgstr "要删除用户，请使用 `rmuser`。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:133
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Looking Around"
msgstr "四处看看"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:136
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Logged in as an ordinary user, look around and try out some commands that "
"will access the sources of help and information within FreeBSD."
msgstr "以普通用户身份登录后，四处看看并试用一些命令，访问 FreeBSD 中的帮助和信息资源。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:138
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here are some commands and what they do:"
msgstr "以下是一些命令及其作用："

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:139
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`id`"
msgstr "`id`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:141
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tells you who you are!"
msgstr "告诉您当前用户是谁！"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:142
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`pwd`"
msgstr "`pwd`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:144
#, fuzzy
msgid "Shows you where you are-the current working directory."
msgstr "显示您所在的位置——当前工作目录。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:145
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`ls`"
msgstr "`ls`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:147
#, fuzzy
msgid "Lists the files in the current directory."
msgstr "列出当前目录中的文件。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:148
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`ls -F`"
msgstr "`ls -F`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:150
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Lists the files in the current directory with a * after executables, a `/` "
"after directories, and an `@` after symbolic links."
msgstr "列出当前目录中的文件；可执行文件后面带有 *，目录后面带有 `/`，符号链接后面带有 `@`。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:151
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`ls -l`"
msgstr "`ls -l`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:153
#, fuzzy
msgid "Lists the files in long format-size, date, permissions."
msgstr "以长格式列出文件——大小、日期和权限。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:154
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`ls -a`"
msgstr "`ls -a`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:157
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Lists hidden \"dot\" files with the others.  If you are `root`, the \"dot\" "
"files show up without the `-a` switch."
msgstr "同时列出隐藏的“点”文件。如果您是 `root`，即使不使用 `-a` 选项，也会显示“点”文件。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:158
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`cd`"
msgstr "`cd`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:162
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Changes directories. `cd ..` backs up one level; note the space after `cd`.  "
"`cd /usr/local` goes there. `cd ~` goes to the home directory of the person "
"logged in-e.g., [.filename]#/usr/home/jack#.  Try `cd /cdrom`, and then "
"`ls`, to find out if your CDROM is mounted and working."
msgstr "切换目录。`cd ..` 返回上一级目录；注意 `cd` 后面有一个空格。`cd /usr/local` 会进入该目录。`cd ~` 会进入当前登录用户的主目录，例如 [.filename]#/usr/home/jack#。试试 `cd /cdrom`，然后运行 `ls`，看看您的 CDROM 是否已挂载并正常工作。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:163
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`less _filename_`"
msgstr "`less __文件名__`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:167
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Lets you look at a file (named _filename_) without changing it.  Try `less /"
"etc/fstab`.  Type `q` to quit."
msgstr "让您查看文件（名为 __文件名__），而不修改它。试试 `less /etc/fstab`。输入 `q` 退出。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:168
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`cat _filename_`"
msgstr "`cat __文件名__`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:173
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Displays _filename_ on screen.  If it is too long and you can see only the "
"end of it, press kbd:[ScrollLock] and use the kbd:[up-arrow] to move "
"backward; you can use kbd:[ScrollLock] with manual pages too.  Press kbd:"
"[ScrollLock] again to quit scrolling.  You might want to try `cat` on some "
"of the dot files in your home directory-`cat .cshrc`, `cat .login`, `cat ."
"profile`."
msgstr "在屏幕上显示 __文件名__。如果内容太长，您只能看到末尾，请按 kbd:[ScrollLock]，再使用 kbd:[up-arrow] 向前滚动；查看手册页时也可以使用 kbd:[ScrollLock]。再次按 kbd:[ScrollLock] 停止滚动。您可以试试用 `cat` 查看主目录中的一些点文件：`cat .cshrc`、`cat .login`、`cat .profile`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:177
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You will notice aliases in [.filename]#.cshrc# for some of the `ls` commands "
"(they are very convenient).  You can create other aliases by editing [."
"filename]#.cshrc#.  You can make these aliases available to all users on the "
"system by putting them in the system-wide `csh` configuration file, [."
"filename]#/etc/csh.cshrc#."
msgstr "您会注意到 [.filename]#.cshrc# 中为一些 `ls` 命令定义了别名（非常方便）。您可以编辑 [.filename]#.cshrc# 来创建其他别名。将这些别名写入系统级的 `csh` 配置文件 [.filename]#/etc/csh.cshrc#，即可让系统中的所有用户都能使用它们。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:179
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Getting Help and Information"
msgstr "获取帮助和信息"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:183
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Here are some useful sources of help.  _Text_ stands for something of your "
"choice that you type in-usually a command or filename."
msgstr "以下是一些有用的帮助来源。__文本__ 表示您自行选择并输入的内容，通常是命令或文件名。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:184
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`apropos _text_`"
msgstr "`apropos __文本__`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:186
#, fuzzy
msgid "Everything containing string _text_ in the `whatis database`."
msgstr "`whatis database` 中所有包含字符串 __文本__ 的内容。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:187
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`man _text_`"
msgstr "`man __文本__`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:192
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The manual page for _text_.  The major source of documentation for UNIX(R) "
"systems.  `man ls` will tell you all the ways to use `ls`.  Press kbd:"
"[Enter] to move through text, kbd:[Ctrl+B] to go back a page, kbd:[Ctrl+F] "
"to go forward, kbd:[q] or kbd:[Ctrl+C] to quit."
msgstr "__文本__ 对应的手册页。它是 UNIX(R) 系统的主要文档来源。`man ls` 会告诉您 `ls` 的各种用法。按 kbd:[Enter] 向下浏览文本，按 kbd:[Ctrl+B] 返回上一页，按 kbd:[Ctrl+F] 前进一页，按 kbd:[q] 或 kbd:[Ctrl+C] 退出。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:193
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`which _text_`"
msgstr "`which __文本__`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:195
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tells you where in the user's path the command _text_ is found."
msgstr "告诉您在用户的搜索路径中，命令 __文本__ 位于何处。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:196
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`locate _text_`"
msgstr "`locate __文本__`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:198
#, fuzzy
msgid "All the paths where the string _text_ is found."
msgstr "列出所有包含字符串 __文本__ 的路径。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:199
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`whatis _text_`"
msgstr "`whatis __文本__`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:202
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Tells you what the command _text_ does and its manual page.  Typing `whatis "
"*` will tell you about all the binaries in the current directory."
msgstr "告诉您命令 __文本__ 的作用及其对应的手册页。输入 `whatis *` 会显示当前目录中所有二进制文件的信息。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:203
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`whereis _text_`"
msgstr "`whereis __文本__`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:205
#, fuzzy
msgid "Finds the file _text_, giving its full path."
msgstr "查找文件 __文本__，并显示其完整路径。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:209
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You might want to try using `whatis` on some common useful commands like "
"`cat`, `more`, `grep`, `mv`, `find`, `tar`, `chmod`, `chown`, `date`, and "
"`script`.  `more` lets you read a page at a time as it does in DOS, e.g., "
"`ls -l | more` or `more _filename_`.  The * works as a wildcard-e.g., `ls "
"w*` will show you files beginning with `w`."
msgstr "您可以试着对一些常用且实用的命令运行 `whatis`，例如 `cat`、`more`、`grep`、`mv`、`find`、`tar`、`chmod`、`chown`、`date` 和 `script`。`more` 可以像 DOS 中那样每次显示一页内容，例如 `ls -l | more` 或 `more __文件名__`。* 可以用作通配符，例如 `ls w*` 会显示以 w 开头的文件。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:213
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Are some of these not working very well? Both man:locate[1] and man:"
"whatis[1] depend on a database that is rebuilt weekly.  If your machine is "
"not going to be left on over the weekend (and running FreeBSD), you might "
"want to run the commands for daily, weekly, and monthly maintenance now and "
"then.  Run them as `root` and, for now, give each one time to finish before "
"you start the next one."
msgstr "其中有些命令是否运行得不太正常？man:locate[1] 和 man:whatis[1] 都依赖一个每周重建的数据库。如果您的计算机周末不会开机并运行 FreeBSD，您可能需要不时手动运行每日、每周和每月维护命令。请以 `root` 身份运行这些命令；目前，请等每条命令运行完毕后再运行下一条。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:222
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# periodic daily\n"
"output omitted\n"
"# periodic weekly\n"
"output omitted\n"
"# periodic monthly\n"
"output omitted\n"
msgstr "# periodic daily\n省略输出\n# periodic weekly\n省略输出\n# periodic monthly\n省略输出\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:228
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If you get tired of waiting, press kbd:[Alt+F2] to get another _virtual "
"console_, and log in again.  After all, it is a multi-user, multi-tasking "
"system.  Nevertheless these commands will probably flash messages on your "
"screen while they are running; you can type `clear` at the prompt to clear "
"the screen.  Once they have run, you might want to look at [.filename]#/var/"
"mail/root# and [.filename]#/var/log/messages#."
msgstr "如果等得不耐烦，可以按 kbd:[Alt+F2] 打开另一个__虚拟控制台__，然后再次登录。毕竟，这是一个多用户、多任务系统。不过，这些命令运行时可能会在屏幕上闪现消息；您可以在提示符下输入 `clear` 清屏。命令运行完后，您可能想查看 [.filename]#/var/mail/root# 和 [.filename]#/var/log/messages#。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:234
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Running such commands is part of system administration-and as a single user "
"of a UNIX(R) system, you are your own system administrator.  Virtually "
"everything you need to be `root` to do is system administration.  Such "
"responsibilities are not covered very well even in those big fat books on "
"UNIX(R), which seem to devote a lot of space to pulling down menus in "
"windows managers.  You might want to get one of the two leading books on "
"systems administration, either Evi Nemeth et.al.'s UNIX System "
"Administration Handbook (Prentice-Hall, 1995, ISBN 0-13-15051-7)-the second "
"edition with the red cover; or Æleen Frisch's Essential System "
"Administration (O'Reilly & Associates, 2002, ISBN 0-596-00343-9).  I used "
"Nemeth."
msgstr "运行这类命令是系统管理工作的一部分——作为 UNIX(R) 系统的唯一用户，您就是自己的系统管理员。几乎所有需要以 `root` 身份执行的操作都属于系统管理。即使那些厚重的 UNIX(R) 书籍也很少详细介绍这些职责；它们似乎把大量篇幅用来讲解窗口管理器中的下拉菜单。您可能想找一本系统管理领域的两本权威著作之一来读：Evi Nemeth 等人编写的《UNIX System Administration Handbook》（Prentice-Hall，1995，ISBN 0-13-15051-7）——第二版，红色封面；或 Æleen Frisch 编写的《Essential System Administration》（O'Reilly & Associates，2002，ISBN 0-596-00343-9）。我用的是 Nemeth 的书。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:236
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Editing Text"
msgstr "编辑文本"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:242
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To configure your system, you need to edit text files.  Most of them will be "
"in the [.filename]#/etc# directory; and you will need to `su` to `root` to "
"be able to change them.  You can use the easy `ee`, but in the long run the "
"text editor `vi` is worth learning.  There is an excellent tutorial on vi in "
"[.filename]#/usr/src/contrib/nvi/docs/tutorial#, if you have the system "
"sources installed."
msgstr "要配置系统，您需要编辑文本文件。其中大多数文件位于 [.filename]#/etc# 目录；要修改它们，您需要使用 `su` 切换为 `root`。您可以使用简单易用的 `ee`，但从长远来看，值得学习文本编辑器 `vi`。如果您安装了系统源代码，可以在 [.filename]#/usr/src/contrib/nvi/docs/tutorial# 找到一篇很棒的 vi 教程。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:246
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Before you edit a file, you should probably back it up.  Suppose you want to "
"edit [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf#.  You could just use `cd /etc` to get to the "
"[.filename]#/etc# directory and do:"
msgstr "编辑文件之前，最好先备份。假设您要编辑 [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf#。您可以使用 `cd /etc` 进入 [.filename]#/etc# 目录，然后运行："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:250
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# cp rc.conf rc.conf.orig\n"
msgstr "# cp rc.conf rc.conf.orig\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:254
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This would copy [.filename]#rc.conf# to [.filename]#rc.conf.orig#, and you "
"could later copy [.filename]#rc.conf.orig# to [.filename]#rc.conf# to "
"recover the original.  But even better would be moving (renaming) and then "
"copying back:"
msgstr "这会将 [.filename]#rc.conf# 复制为 [.filename]#rc.conf.orig#；之后您可以将 [.filename]#rc.conf.orig# 复制回 [.filename]#rc.conf# 来恢复原文件。不过，更好的做法是先移动（重命名）原文件，再复制回来："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:259
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# mv rc.conf rc.conf.orig\n"
"# cp rc.conf.orig rc.conf\n"
msgstr "# mv rc.conf rc.conf.orig\n# cp rc.conf.orig rc.conf\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:264
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"because `mv` preserves the original date and owner of the file.  You can now "
"edit [.filename]#rc.conf#.  If you want the original back, you would then "
"`mv rc.conf rc.conf.myedit` (assuming you want to preserve your edited "
"version) and then"
msgstr "因为 `mv` 会保留原文件的日期和所有者。现在您可以编辑 [.filename]#rc.conf#。如果要恢复原文件，可以先运行 `mv rc.conf rc.conf.myedit`（假设您想保留修改后的版本），然后运行："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:268
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# mv rc.conf.orig rc.conf\n"
msgstr "# mv rc.conf.orig rc.conf\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:271
#, fuzzy
msgid "to put things back the way they were."
msgstr "这样就能恢复原状。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:273
#, fuzzy
msgid "To edit a file, type"
msgstr "要编辑文件，请输入"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:277
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# vi filename\n"
msgstr "# vi filename\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:282
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Move through the text with the arrow keys.  kbd:[Esc] (the escape key) puts "
"`vi` in command mode.  Here are some commands:"
msgstr "使用方向键在文本中移动。kbd:[Esc]（退出键）会让 `vi` 进入命令模式。以下是一些命令："

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:283
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`x`"
msgstr "`x`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:285
#, fuzzy
msgid "delete letter the cursor is on"
msgstr "删除光标所在的字符"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:286
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`dd`"
msgstr "`dd`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:288
#, fuzzy
msgid "delete the entire line (even if it wraps on the screen)"
msgstr "删除整行（即使该行在屏幕上显示为多行）"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:289
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`i`"
msgstr "`i`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:291
#, fuzzy
msgid "insert text at the cursor"
msgstr "在光标处插入文本"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:292
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`a`"
msgstr "`a`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:294
#, fuzzy
msgid "insert text after the cursor"
msgstr "在光标后插入文本"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:297
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once you type `i` or `a`, you can enter text.  `Esc` puts you back in "
"command mode where you can type"
msgstr "输入 `i` 或 `a` 后，即可输入文本。按 `Esc` 返回命令模式，然后可以输入"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:298
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`:w`"
msgstr "`:w`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:300
#, fuzzy
msgid "to write your changes to disk and continue editing"
msgstr "将修改写入磁盘并继续编辑"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:301
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`:wq`"
msgstr "`:wq`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:303
#, fuzzy
msgid "to write and quit"
msgstr "保存并退出"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:304
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`:q!`"
msgstr "`:q!`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:306
#, fuzzy
msgid "to quit without saving changes"
msgstr "不保存修改并退出"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:307
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`/_text_`"
msgstr "`/_text_`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:309
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"to move the cursor to _text_; `/` kbd:[Enter] (the enter key) to find the "
"next instance of _text_."
msgstr "将光标移至 __文本__；输入 `/` 并按 kbd:[Enter]（回车键）可查找 __文本__ 的下一个匹配项。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:310
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`G`"
msgstr "`G`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:312
#, fuzzy
msgid "to go to the end of the file"
msgstr "跳转到文件末尾"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:313
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`nG`"
msgstr "`nG`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:315
#, fuzzy
msgid "to go to line _n_ in the file, where _n_ is a number"
msgstr "跳转到文件中的第 _n_ 行，其中 _n_ 是一个数字"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:316
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "kbd:[Ctrl+L]"
msgstr "kbd:[Ctrl+L]"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:318
#, fuzzy
msgid "to redraw the screen"
msgstr "重绘屏幕"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:319
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "kbd:[Ctrl+b] and kbd:[Ctrl+f]"
msgstr "kbd:[Ctrl+b] 和 kbd:[Ctrl+f]"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:321
#, fuzzy
msgid "go back and forward a screen, as they do with `more` and `view`."
msgstr "像使用 `more` 和 `view` 时那样，向后或向前翻一屏。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:326
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Practice with `vi` in your home directory by creating a new file with `vi "
"_filename_` and adding and deleting text, saving the file, and calling it up "
"again.  `vi` delivers some surprises because it is really quite complex, and "
"sometimes you will inadvertently issue a command that will do something you "
"do not expect.  (Some people actually like `vi`-it is more powerful than DOS "
"EDIT-find out about `:r`.)  Use kbd:[Esc] one or more times to be sure you "
"are in command mode and proceed from there when it gives you trouble, save "
"often with `:w`, and use `:q!` to get out and start over (from your last `:"
"w`) when you need to."
msgstr "在主目录中练习使用 `vi`：用 `vi _filename_` 创建一个新文件，添加和删除文本，保存文件，然后再次打开它。`vi` 会带来一些意外，因为它确实相当复杂，有时你会无意中发出一条执行结果出乎意料的命令。（有些人确实喜欢 `vi`——它比 DOS EDIT 更强大，不妨了解一下 `:r`。）遇到问题时，按一次或多次 kbd:[Esc]，确保处于命令模式，然后从那里继续；经常用 `:w` 保存，需要时用 `:q!` 退出并从上次 `:w` 保存的状态重新开始。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:330
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Now you can `cd` to [.filename]#/etc#, `su` to `root`, use `vi` to edit the "
"file [.filename]#/etc/group#, and add a user to `wheel` so the user has root "
"privileges.  Just add a comma and the user's login name to the end of the "
"first line in the file, press kbd:[Esc], and use `:wq` to write the file to "
"disk and quit.  Instantly effective. (You did not put a space after the "
"comma, did you?)"
msgstr "现在，你可以用 `cd` 进入 [.filename]#/etc#，用 `su` 切换到 `root`，使用 `vi` 编辑 [.filename]#/etc/group#，并将一个用户添加到 `wheel`，使其拥有 root 权限。只需在文件第一行末尾添加一个逗号和该用户的登录名，按 kbd:[Esc]，再用 `:wq` 将文件写入磁盘并退出。更改会立即生效。（你没有在逗号后面加空格，对吧？）"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:332
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Other Useful Commands"
msgstr "其他有用的命令"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:334
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`df`"
msgstr "`df`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:336
#, fuzzy
msgid "shows file space and mounted systems."
msgstr "显示文件系统空间和已挂载的文件系统。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:337
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`ps aux`"
msgstr "`ps aux`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:339
#, fuzzy
msgid "shows processes running. `ps ax` is a narrower form."
msgstr "显示正在运行的进程。`ps ax` 是范围较窄的形式。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:340
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`rm _filename_`"
msgstr "`rm _filename_`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:342
#, fuzzy
msgid "remove _filename_."
msgstr "删除 _filename_。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:343
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`rm -R _dir_`"
msgstr "`rm -R _dir_`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:345
#, fuzzy
msgid "removes a directory _dir_ and all subdirectories-careful!"
msgstr "删除目录 _dir_ 及其所有子目录——务必小心！"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:346
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`ls -R`"
msgstr "`ls -R`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:348
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"lists files in the current directory and all subdirectories; I used a "
"variant, `ls -AFR > where.txt`, to get a list of all the files in [."
"filename]#/# and (separately) [.filename]#/usr# before I found better ways "
"to find files."
msgstr "列出当前目录及所有子目录中的文件；我曾使用一个变体 `ls -AFR > where.txt`，在找到更好的查找文件方法之前，用它分别列出 [.filename]#/# 和 [.filename]#/usr# 中的所有文件。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:349
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`passwd`"
msgstr "`passwd`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:351
#, fuzzy
msgid "to change user's password (or ``root``'s password)"
msgstr "更改用户密码（或 ``root`` 的密码）"

#. type: Labeled list
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:352
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`man hier`"
msgstr "`man hier`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:354
#, fuzzy
msgid "manual page on the UNIX(R) filesystem"
msgstr "关于 UNIX(R) 文件系统的手册页"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:356
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Use `find` to locate [.filename]#filename# in [.filename]#/usr# or any of "
"its subdirectories with"
msgstr "使用 `find` 在 [.filename]#/usr# 或其任意子目录中查找 [.filename]#filename#："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:360
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% find /usr -name \"filename\"\n"
msgstr "% find /usr -name \"filename\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:364
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You can use * as a wildcard in `\"_filename_\"` (which should be in "
"quotes).  If you tell `find` to search in [.filename]#/# instead of [."
"filename]#/usr# it will look for the file(s) on all mounted filesystems, "
"including the CDROM and the DOS partition."
msgstr "你可以在 `\"_filename_\"` 中使用 * 作为通配符（应将其放在引号中）。如果让 `find` 在 [.filename]#/# 而不是 [.filename]#/usr# 中搜索，它会在所有已挂载的文件系统中查找文件，包括 CDROM 和 DOS 分区。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:366
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"An excellent book that explains UNIX(R) commands and utilities is Abrahams & "
"Larson, Unix for the Impatient (2nd ed., Addison-Wesley, 1996). There is "
"also a lot of UNIX(R) information on the Internet."
msgstr "一本非常出色的 UNIX(R) 命令和实用工具入门书是 Abrahams & Larson 所著的《Unix for the Impatient》（第 2 版，Addison-Wesley，1996 年）。互联网上也有大量 UNIX(R) 相关信息。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:368
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Next Steps"
msgstr "接下来的步骤"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:375
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You should now have the tools you need to get around and edit files, so you "
"can get everything up and running.  There is a great deal of information in "
"the FreeBSD handbook (which is probably on your hard drive) and link:https://"
"www.FreeBSD.org/[FreeBSD's web site].  A wide variety of packages and ports "
"are on the CDROM as well as the web site.  The handbook tells you more about "
"how to use them (get the package if it exists, with `pkg add _packagename_`, "
"where _packagename_ is the filename of the package).  The CDROM has lists of "
"the packages and ports with brief descriptions in [.filename]#cdrom/packages/"
"index#, [.filename]#cdrom/packages/index.txt#, and [.filename]#cdrom/ports/"
"index#, with fuller descriptions in [.filename]#/cdrom/ports/\\*/*/pkg/"
"DESCR#, where the *s represent subdirectories of kinds of programs and "
"program names respectively."
msgstr "现在，你应该已经具备了浏览系统和编辑文件所需的工具，可以开始让一切运行起来了。FreeBSD 手册（很可能就在你的硬盘上）以及 link:https://www.FreeBSD.org/[FreeBSD 网站]都包含大量信息。CDROM 和网站上还有各种各样的软件包和 Ports。手册会进一步介绍如何使用它们（如果存在相应的软件包，就获取该软件包，使用 `pkg add _packagename_`，其中 _packagename_ 是软件包的文件名）。CDROM 上的 [.filename]#cdrom/packages/index#、[.filename]#cdrom/packages/index.txt# 和 [.filename]#cdrom/ports/index# 中列有软件包和 Ports，并附有简短说明；更详细的说明位于 [.filename]#/cdrom/ports/\\*/*/pkg/DESCR#，其中两个 * 分别代表程序类别和程序名称的子目录。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:377
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If you find the handbook too sophisticated (what with `lndir` and all) on "
"installing ports from the CDROM, here is what usually works:"
msgstr "如果手册中关于从 CDROM 安装 Ports 的说明过于复杂（涉及 `lndir` 等内容），下面介绍一种通常可行的方法："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:380
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Find the port you want, say `kermit`. There will be a directory for it on "
"the CDROM.  Copy the subdirectory to [.filename]#/usr/local# (a good place "
"for software you add that should be available to all users) with:"
msgstr "找到你想要的 Port，例如 `kermit`。CDROM 上会有一个对应目录。用以下命令将该子目录复制到 [.filename]#/usr/local#（这是存放你添加的软件的好位置，所有用户都可以使用）："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:384
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# cp -R /cdrom/ports/comm/kermit /usr/local\n"
msgstr "# cp -R /cdrom/ports/comm/kermit /usr/local\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:387
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This should result in a [.filename]#/usr/local/kermit# subdirectory that has "
"all the files that the `kermit` subdirectory on the CDROM has."
msgstr "这样应该会生成 [.filename]#/usr/local/kermit# 子目录，其中包含 CDROM 上 `kermit` 子目录里的所有文件。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:392
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Next, create the directory [.filename]#/usr/ports/distfiles# if it does not "
"already exist using `mkdir`.  Now check [.filename]#/cdrom/ports/distfiles# "
"for a file with a name that indicates it is the port you want.  Copy that "
"file to [.filename]#/usr/ports/distfiles#; in recent versions you can skip "
"this step, as FreeBSD will do it for you.  In the case of `kermit`, there is "
"no distfile."
msgstr "接下来，如果 [.filename]#/usr/ports/distfiles# 目录尚不存在，就用 `mkdir` 创建它。然后检查 [.filename]#/cdrom/ports/distfiles# 中是否有文件名表明它是你需要的 Port 的文件。将该文件复制到 [.filename]#/usr/ports/distfiles#；在较新的版本中可以跳过这一步，因为 FreeBSD 会自动完成。在 `kermit` 的例子中，没有 distfile。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:395
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Then `cd` to the subdirectory of [.filename]#/usr/local/kermit# that has the "
"file [.filename]#Makefile#.  Type"
msgstr "然后用 `cd` 进入 [.filename]#/usr/local/kermit# 中包含 [.filename]#Makefile# 文件的子目录。输入"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:399
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# make all install\n"
msgstr "# make all install\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:405
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"During this process the port will FTP to get any compressed files it needs "
"that it did not find on the CDROM or in [.filename]#/usr/ports/distfiles#.  "
"If you do not have your network running yet and there was no file for the "
"port in [.filename]#/cdrom/ports/distfiles#, you will have to get the "
"distfile using another machine and copy it to [.filename]#/usr/ports/"
"distfiles#.  Read [.filename]#Makefile# (with `cat` or `more` or `view`) to "
"find out where to go (the master distribution site) to get the file and what "
"its name is.  (Use binary file transfers!) Then go back to [.filename]#/usr/"
"local/kermit#, find the directory with [.filename]#Makefile#, and type `make "
"all install`."
msgstr "在此过程中，Port 会通过 FTP 获取它所需、但在 CDROM 或 [.filename]#/usr/ports/distfiles# 中找不到的压缩文件。如果你的网络尚未配置好，并且 [.filename]#/cdrom/ports/distfiles# 中也没有该 Port 所需的文件，你就必须用另一台计算机获取 distfile，再将其复制到 [.filename]#/usr/ports/distfiles#。阅读 [.filename]#Makefile#（使用 `cat`、`more` 或 `view`）以查找获取该文件的地址（主分发站点）和文件名。（请使用二进制文件传输！）然后回到 [.filename]#/usr/local/kermit#，找到含有 [.filename]#Makefile# 的目录，并输入 `make all install`。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:407
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Your Working Environment"
msgstr "你的工作环境"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:412
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Your shell is the most important part of your working environment.  The "
"shell is what interprets the commands you type on the command line, and thus "
"communicates with the rest of the operating system.  You can also write "
"shell scripts a series of commands to be run without intervention."
msgstr "Shell 是工作环境中最重要的部分。Shell 负责解释你在命令行输入的命令，因此也负责与操作系统的其余部分进行通信。你还可以编写 Shell 脚本，也就是一系列无需人工干预即可运行的命令。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:416
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Two shells come installed with FreeBSD: `csh` and `sh`.  `csh` is good for "
"command-line work, but scripts should be written with `sh` (or `bash`).  You "
"can find out what shell you have by typing `echo $SHELL`."
msgstr "FreeBSD 随系统安装了两个 Shell：`csh` 和 `sh`。`csh` 适合在命令行中工作，但脚本应使用 `sh`（或 `bash`）编写。输入 `echo $SHELL` 可以查看你当前使用的 Shell。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:422
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `csh` shell is okay, but `tcsh` does everything `csh` does and more.  It "
"allows you to recall commands with the arrow keys and edit them.  It has tab-"
"key completion of filenames (`csh` uses kbd:[Esc]), and it lets you switch "
"to the directory you were last in with `cd -`.  It is also much easier to "
"alter your prompt with `tcsh`.  It makes life a lot easier."
msgstr "`csh` 还不错，但 `tcsh` 除了具备 `csh` 的所有功能，还提供了更多功能。它允许你用方向键调出命令并编辑命令。它支持按 Tab 键补全文件名（`csh` 使用 kbd:[Esc]），还可以用 `cd -` 切换到你上次所在的目录。使用 `tcsh` 修改提示符也容易得多。它会让生活轻松许多。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:424
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here are the three steps for installing a new shell:"
msgstr "安装新 Shell 分为以下三个步骤："

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:428
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Install the shell as a port or a package, just as you would any other port "
"or package."
msgstr "像安装其他 Port 或软件包一样，将该 Shell 作为 Port 或软件包安装。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:429
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Use `chsh` to change your shell to `tcsh` permanently, or type `tcsh` at the "
"prompt to change your shell without logging in again."
msgstr "使用 `chsh` 将你的 Shell 永久更改为 `tcsh`，或者在提示符下输入 `tcsh`，无需重新登录即可切换 Shell。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:437
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"It can be dangerous to change `root`'s shell to something other than `sh` or "
"`csh` on early versions of FreeBSD and many other versions of UNIX(R); you "
"may not have a working shell when the system puts you into single user "
"mode.  The solution is to use `su -m` to become `root`, which will give you "
"the `tcsh` as `root`, because the shell is part of the environment.  You can "
"make this permanent by adding it to your [.filename]#.tcshrc# as an alias "
"with:"
msgstr "在早期版本的 FreeBSD 和许多其他版本的 UNIX(R) 中，将 `root` 的 Shell 更改为 `sh` 或 `csh` 以外的 Shell 可能会有危险；系统进入单用户模式时，你可能会遇到无法正常使用的 Shell。解决方法是使用 `su -m` 切换到 `root`，这样 `root` 就会使用你的 `tcsh`，因为 Shell 是环境的一部分。你可以将以下别名添加到 [.filename]#.tcshrc# 中，使此设置永久生效："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:441
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "alias su su -m\n"
msgstr "alias su su -m\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:448
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When `tcsh` starts up, it will read the [.filename]#/etc/csh.cshrc# and [."
"filename]#/etc/csh.login# files, as does `csh`.  It will also read [."
"filename]#.login# in your home directory and [.filename]#.cshrc# as well, "
"unless you provide a [.filename]#.tcshrc#.  This you can do by simply "
"copying [.filename]#.cshrc# to [.filename]#.tcshrc#."
msgstr "`tcsh` 启动时会读取 [.filename]#/etc/csh.cshrc# 和 [.filename]#/etc/csh.login# 文件，就像 `csh` 一样。它还会读取你主目录中的 [.filename]#.login# 和 [.filename]#.cshrc#，除非你提供了 [.filename]#.tcshrc#。只需将 [.filename]#.cshrc# 复制为 [.filename]#.tcshrc# 即可。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:452
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Now that you have installed `tcsh`, you can adjust your prompt.  You can "
"find the details in the manual page for `tcsh`, but here is a line to put in "
"your [.filename]#.tcshrc# that will tell you how many commands you have "
"typed, what time it is, and what directory you are in.  It also produces a "
"`>` if you are an ordinary user and a # if you are `root`, but tsch will do "
"that in any case:"
msgstr "安装好 `tcsh` 后，你可以调整提示符。详细信息请参阅 `tcsh` 的手册页；这里提供一行内容，将它放入 [.filename]#.tcshrc# 后，就能显示你输入过的命令数、当前时间和所在目录。如果你是普通用户，它还会显示 `>`；如果你是 `root`，则显示 #。不过 tsch 无论如何都会这样做："

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:454
#, fuzzy
msgid "set prompt = \"%h %t %~ %# \""
msgstr "set prompt = \"%h %t %~ %# \""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:459
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This should go in the same place as the existing set prompt line if there is "
"one, or under \"if($?prompt) then\" if not.  Comment out the old line; you "
"can always switch back to it if you prefer it.  Do not forget the spaces and "
"quotes.  You can get the [.filename]#.tcshrc# reread by typing `source ."
"tcshrc`."
msgstr "如果已有 `set prompt` 行，就把这行放在同一位置；如果没有，就把它放在 `if($?prompt) then` 下面。将旧行注释掉；如果你更喜欢旧设置，随时可以切换回去。不要忘记空格和引号。输入 `source .tcshrc` 可以重新读取 [.filename]#.tcshrc#。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:463
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You can get a listing of other environmental variables that have been set by "
"typing `env` at the prompt.  The result will show you your default editor, "
"pager, and terminal type, among possibly many others.  A useful command if "
"you log in from a remote location and cannot run a program because the "
"terminal is not capable is `setenv TERM vt100`."
msgstr "在提示符下输入 `env`，可以查看已设置的其他环境变量。结果会显示你的默认编辑器、分页程序和终端类型等信息。如果你从远程位置登录，并且由于终端功能不足而无法运行某个程序，可以使用以下命令：`setenv TERM vt100`。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:465
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other"
msgstr "其他"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:469
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"As `root`, you can unmount the CDROM with `/sbin/umount /cdrom`, take it out "
"of the drive, insert another one, and mount it with `/sbin/mount_cd9660 /dev/"
"cd0a /cdrom` assuming cd0a is the device name for your CDROM drive.  The "
"most recent versions of FreeBSD let you mount the CDROM with just `/sbin/"
"mount /cdrom`."
msgstr "作为 `root`，你可以用 `/sbin/umount /cdrom` 卸载 CDROM，将其取出并放入另一张光盘，然后用 `/sbin/mount_cd9660 /dev/cd0a /cdrom` 挂载；这里假设你的 CDROM 驱动器设备名是 cd0a。最新版本的 FreeBSD 允许你只用 `/sbin/mount /cdrom` 挂载 CDROM。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/new-users/_index.adoc:475
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Using the live filesystem-the second of FreeBSD's CDROM disks-is useful if "
"you have got limited space.  What is on the live filesystem varies from "
"release to release.  You might try playing games from the CDROM.  This "
"involves using `lndir`, which gets installed with the X Window System, to "
"tell the program(s) where to find the necessary files, because they are in [."
"filename]#/cdrom# instead of in [.filename]#/usr# and its subdirectories, "
"which is where they are expected to be.  Read `man lndir`."
msgstr "如果空间有限，使用实时文件系统（FreeBSD 第二张 CDROM 光盘）会很有用。实时文件系统中的内容因发行版而异。你可以尝试从 CDROM 运行游戏。这需要使用随 X Window System 安装的 `lndir`，告诉程序到哪里查找所需文件，因为这些文件位于 [.filename]#/cdrom#，而不是程序预期的 [.filename]#/usr# 及其子目录中。请阅读 `man lndir`。"

